      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "Find $3det(A)-4det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6\\sqrt{2} & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- For the matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=7\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 4=-5.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6\\sqrt{2} & 10\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3det(A)-4det(B)=3\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot 0=-15.$",
